ations and memories, newest first. | Optional `session_id`, `limit`. | Memory list excluding invalidated records. | Structured response. | `limit` bounds results. | generic events. | Redesigned-with-shim. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |\n| `list_stale_memories` | Lists stale memories likely needing review or refresh. | Optional `query`, `limit`. | Stale memory candidates. | Structured response. | `limit` bounds results. | generic events. | Stable canonical. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |\n| `promote_observation` | Promotes session memory into branch or repo scope with metadata. | `id`, `scope` required; optional links, workspace, branch, `refresh_key`. | Promotion result and updated metadata. | Structured response. | No explicit budget. | generic events; memory write path. | Redesigned-with-shim. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |\n| `refresh_memory` | Refreshes memory evidence and metadata while preserving identity and clearing stale state. | `id` required; optional content, type, scope, links, workspace, branch, freshness, confidence. | Updated memory metadata. | Structured response. | No explicit budget. | generic events; memory update path. | Stable canonical. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |\n| `delete_observation` | Deletes a stored observation by id. | `id` required. | Delete confirmation. | Structured response. | No explicit budget. | generic events; memory lifecycle path. | Redesigned-with-shim. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |\n| `update_observation` | Updates observation content in place and clears stale flags. | `id`, `content` required. | Updated memory metadata. | Structured response. | No explicit budget. | generic events; memory update path. | Redesigned-with-shim. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |\n| `consolidate_session` | Triggers proposal-only session consolidation and returns auditable proposal ids. | `session_id` required; optional `mode`, `budget_ms`, `render_mode`. | Consolidation report with proposals, categories, incomplete flag, and notes. | `render_mode=compact/full/diagnostic`. | `budget_ms`; render mode bounds detail. | generic events; `MemoryConsolidated`. | Stable canonical Phase 8 memory tool. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/consolidate_session.rs` |\n| `get_memory_metrics` | Returns Phase 9 memory and workflow metrics with provenance and honest nulls for unavailable signals. | Optional `scope`, `time_range`, `signals`, `render_mode`. | Metric snapshot with requested signals, values, provenance, and availability. | `render_mode=compact/full/diagnostic`. | Requested `signals` and render mode bound payload. | generic events. | Stable canonical Phase 8 memory tool. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/get_memory_metrics.rs` |\n| `get_event_trace` | Returns paginated, workspace-bounded event traces for task, session, or workspace scopes. | Optional `task_id`, `session_id`, `workspace_id`, `kinds`, `since`, `until`, `cursor`, `limit`, `render_mode`. | Event page with scope, events, cursor, payloads in full/diagnostic, hashes in diagnostic. | `render_mode=compact/full/diagnostic`; event expansion handles. | `limit`, cursor pagination, filters, render mode. | generic events; returns event records. | Stable canonical Phase 8 memory tool. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/get_event_trace.rs` |\n| `get_task_memory` | Reads working memory plus relevant durable memory for the current task. | `task_id` required; optional `intent_hint`, `budget_tokens`. | Task memory bundle with inclusion reasons, verification/freshness/conflict state, and expansion handles. | Full structured bundle with memory expansion handles. | `budget_tokens` clips memory payload. | generic events; `MemoryRetrieved`. | Stable canonical Phase 8 memory tool. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/get_task_memory.rs` |\n| `save_memory` | Creates a durable memory with evidence, validity conditions, invalidation triggers, and queued verification. | Memory content/type/scope/evidence/link fields; validation requires a meaningful claim and scope. | Created memory response with metadata, verification state, and expansion handle. | Structured response. | No explicit budget. | generic events; `MemoryCreated`. | Stable canonical Phase 8 memory tool. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/save_memory.rs` |\n| `propose_memory_evolution` | Persists, applies, or rejects auditable memory-evolution proposals. | `action` required; proposal actions accept `proposal_id`, `memory_id`, content, links, validity, invalidation, supersession, reason, and actor fields as applicable. | Evolution proposal/result with proposal id, action, proposed memory state, decision metadata, and optional deprecation warning for shimmed calls. | Structured response. | No explicit budget. | generic events; apply/reject emits consolidation/update lifecycle through memory path. | Stable canonical Phase 8 memory tool. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/propose_memory_evolution.rs` |\n| `apply_memory_evolution` | Deprecated advertised shim for applying an existing evolution proposal. | `proposal_id` required; optional `reason`, `decided_by`. | Same result as `propose_memory_evolution(action=\"apply\")` plus `deprecation_warning`. | Structured response. | No explicit budget. | generic events; canonical action path. | Deprecated shim; remove per compatibility policy. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/propose_memory_evolution.rs` |\n| `verify_explain_memory` | Runs fresh verification checks for a durable memory or explains the last persisted report. | `memory_id` required; optional `mode`, `render_mode`. | Verification status, checks, confidence delta, expansion handle, summary lines, optional diagnostic trace. | `mode=verify/explain/verify_and_explain`; `render_mode=compact/full/diagnostic`; expansion handle. | Render mode bounds detail. | generic events; verification memory retrieval/invalidation as applicable. | Stable canonical Phase 8 memory tool. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/verify_explain_memory.rs` |\n| `verify_memory` | Deprecated advertised shim for verification-only mode. | Same as `verify_explain_memory`; shim forces `mode=verify`. | Same response as canonical verify mode plus `deprecation_warning`. | `render_mode=compact/full/diagnostic`; expansion handle. | Render mode bounds detail. | generic events; canonical mode path. | Deprecated shim; remove per compatibility policy. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/verify_explain_memory.rs` |\n| `explain_memory` | Deprecated advertised shim for explanation-only mode. | Same as `verify_explain_memory`; shim forces `mode=explain`. | Same response as canonical explain mode plus `deprecation_warning`. | `render_mode=compact/full/diagnostic`; expansion handle. | Render mode bounds detail. | generic events; canonical mode path. | Deprecated shim; remove per compatibility policy. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/verify_explain_memory.rs` |\n| `list_memory_conflicts` | Lists contradiction and supersession edges anchored on a memory or graph node. | Anchor identity or legacy memory id; optional scope, pagination, and `render_mode`. | Conflict page with anchors, edges, summaries, and pagination. | `render_mode=compact/full/diagnostic`. | Pagination and render mode bound payload. | generic events. | Stable canonical Phase 8 memory tool. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/list_memory_conflicts.rs` |\n\n### Callable deprecated aliases\n\nThese names are accepted by `handle_tools_call` but are not advertised in `tools/list`. They remain compatibility debt governed by [## Legacy aliases and deadlines](./2026-05-16-mcp-compatibility-policy.md#legacy-aliases-and-deadlines) and [## Shim removal protocol](./2026-05-16-mcp-compatibility-policy.md#shim-removal-protocol).\n\n| Alias | Canonical target | Request and response compatibility | Events | Implementing file |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `query_context` | `get_context_capsule` | Accepts the legacy context-query request and returns the canonical context capsule shape. | generic events under alias name. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |\n| `blast_radius` | `get_impact_graph` | Accepts the legacy impact request and returns impact graph output. | generic events under alias name. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |\n| `get_file_context` | `get_skeleton` | Accepts the legacy file-context request and returns skeleton output. | generic events under alias name. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |\n| `store_memory` | `save_observation` | Accepts the legacy memory-store request and returns observation memory output. | generic events under alias name. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |\n| `recall_memories` | `search_memory` | Accepts the legacy recall request and returns memory search output. | generic events under alias name. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |\n\n## Render modes\n\n[## MCP Surface](../plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#mcp-surface) requires compact rendering, full structured JSON, context handles, stable expansion targets, budget controls, and diagnostic explanations where useful. [## MCP Tool Contract Principles](../plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#mcp-tool-contract-principles) requires compact/full render choice and structured payloads.\n\nWorkflow tools use `render=json|markdown|hybrid` for delivery shape and `mode=auto|compact|full` when a workflow bundle supports response density. `get_context_capsule` keeps its older `mode=full|focused` discovery control. Memory v2 administrative tools use `render_mode=compact|full|diagnostic`; `verify_explain_memory` additionally uses `mode=verify|explain|verify_and_explain`.\n\nDiagnostic render modes are reserved for traceability: they may include check traces, ranking reasons, payload hashes, spilled-payload row ids, or excluded candidates. Compact modes must remain bounded enough for repeated assistant use.\n\n## Expansion handles\n\nWorkflow responses that return bundles store context handles through `context_cache` and expose `suggested_expand` targets. `expand_context` is the canonical follow-up tool and accepts a prior `handle` plus a `focus` such as a file, symbol, test, memory, or stable identity. Memory-bearing responses expose memory or event expansion handles where useful: `get_task_memory`, `verify_explain_memory`, `get_event_trace`, and `inspect_working_memory` all return handles for focused follow-up.\n\nHandles must stay workspace-bound and must not bypass the path scoping, ignored-directory rules, or memory scoping required by the repo contract. Expired, missing, or invalid handles should fail with actionable errors rather than silently returning unrelated context.\n\n## Budget controls\n\nBudget controls are part of the MCP contract in [## MCP Surface](../plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#mcp-surface). Workflow bundle tools accept `budget=tiny|compact|full`, `max_tokens`, and `wire_format=standard|dense` where listed. The daemon constants are `tiny=260`, `compact=850`, and `full=2600` approximate workflow token caps unless a stricter `max_tokens` is supplied.\n\nOther tools expose narrower controls: `limit` bounds list/search/event outputs, `hops` and `max_depth` bound graph traversal, `budget_tokens` bounds `get_task_memory`, `budget_ms` bounds synchronous consolidation, cursor pagination bounds `get_event_trace`, and render modes bound diagnostic detail.\n\n## Deprecation policy\n\nDeprecation follows [## Backward compatibility](./2026-05-16-mcp-compatibility-policy.md#backward-compatibility) and [## Shim removal protocol](./2026-05-16-mcp-compatibility-policy.md#shim-removal-protocol). A redesigned tool must keep maintained clients working for one full numbered phase cycle. The legacy request shape must remain accepted, responses must remain parseable, and new identity/event/ranking/memory fields must be additive unless a shim explicitly documents a successor contract.\n\nThe Phase 8 advertised deprecated shims are `apply_memory_evolution`, `verify_memory`, and `explain_memory`. The callable-only legacy aliases are `query_context`, `blast_radius`, `get_file_context`, `store_memory`, and `recall_memories`. Removal requires a phase boundary, migrated first-party docs/fixtures/prompts/cached examples, compatibility tests, and an architecture-doc update in the same change.\n","numLines":100,"startLine":1,"totalLines":100}}}
